{
  "requirement": "Usage MUST record each provider request's outcome and available input/output\ntoken counts, including retries, with cached or reasoning-token counts when\nprovided, and for a failed request the failure under\n{cite}`requirements.authoring.usage_requests.failures`. Missing measurements MUST be recorded as unavailable, not zero.\nRun totals MUST include request and tool-call counts by tool, elapsed time, and\navailable token usage, identifying incomplete totals without double counting\nprovider counters that overlap.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.authoring.usage_requests`. Each obligation maps to a test with assertions that enforce it.\n\n**Per-request outcome and input/output tokens, including retries**\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[throttled_requests_retry_unchanged_and_record_every_attempt]` forces 5 throttled failures and then a success. It asserts `request_count` is 6, the first five outcomes are `failed`, and the sixth is `completed`.\n- `unanswered_requests_are_abandoned_and_retried` asserts an abandoned request is recorded as `failed` and its retry as `completed`.\n- `success_resets_backoff_and_retries_keep_history_without_repeating_tools` asserts 4 requests and one `habeas` tool call across retries.\n- `src/authoring/providers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bedrock_sdk_retries_are_disabled]` asserts `max_attempts` is 1. This keeps every provider attempt visible as its own recorded request.\n- The CLI tests `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free` and `bedrock_cli_uses_selected_profile_region_and_converse_tools` assert end-to-end token totals (33/21 and 38/10) and `request_count`.\n\n**Cached and reasoning tokens when provided**\n- `token_totals_keep_subsets_separate_and_missing_counters_unknown` asserts per-request and total cached, cache-creation and reasoning counts.\n- `claude_requests_carry_cache_checkpoints_and_record_cache_usage` asserts cached and cache-creation counts per request and in total.\n- `openai_responses_replays_tool_calls_and_records_usage` asserts cached (6) and reasoning (4) totals.\n\n**Missing measurements recorded as unavailable, not zero**\n- `token_totals_keep_subsets_separate_and_missing_counters_unknown` asserts a failed request's per-request `input` is null.\n- `partial_failure_retains_available_totals_and_optional_measurements` asserts an unreported `cached_input` is null while an explicit `cached_input_tokens(0)` stays 0. It also asserts an unmeasured `reasoning` total is null.\n- `tool_outcomes_are_distinct_and_unknown_names_do_not_leak_model_text` asserts the run `tokens.input` is null when no request exists.\n\n**Failed-request failure details**\n- This is delegated to the cited `requirements.authoring.usage_requests.failures`, so I did not reassess it. The throttled test and `failed_submission_can_be_confirmed_on_a_later_attempt` nonetheless assert the failure object and its `retried` flag.\n\n**Run totals**\n- Request counts are asserted in the tests above.\n- Tool-call counts by tool, plus failures and skips, are asserted in `tool_outcomes_are_distinct_and_unknown_names_do_not_leak_model_text`. The CLI test asserts them end to end.\n- Elapsed time is covered by `completed_requests_and_the_run_record_elapsed_time`. It asserts the per-request value (20 ms), the run's `elapsed_ms` of at least 50 ms mid-run and after `finish`, and that the run value is at least the request value. `cancelled_request_persists_elapsed_time_and_incomplete_totals` asserts a cancelled request's elapsed time.\n- Incomplete totals are identified through the `tokens.complete` flag. `token_totals_keep_subsets_separate_and_missing_counters_unknown` asserts it is false while a request is in flight and true once all requests finish. The partial-failure, cancelled and failed-run tests assert it is false.\n\n**No double counting of overlapping counters**\n- In `token_totals_keep_subsets_separate_and_missing_counters_unknown`, two requests each report input 100 with cached 30. The test asserts total input is 200 and cached is 60, so cached tokens are not added into input.\n- The OpenAI CLI test asserts input stays 22 while cached is 6.\n\nI found no obligation without a test.",
  "references": "80b6e1f44e7d0ffb649a06075f03bca8679bd50e3a1b7bec591b84e04e66629e",
